      "writtenOn": "2023-07-05T19:56:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My only objection is that the comment describes the effect of the code using inverse terminology from what the code is doing, which could make it confusing the understand later. The most direct interpretation of the code is \"disable the unaligned access trap by clearing the associated bit in the NVIC_CCR register\". The net effect does allow you to use unaligned access without a trap but this is performed by \"disabling the trap\" (clearing a bit) rather than by \"enabling a feature\". I could see future readers (i.e. two years from now) reading this and being confused about why `REGISTER \u0026\u003d ~BIT_DEFINITION` is \"enabling\" something.",
      "parentUuid": "4497cc14_03fec67d",
